; Exports for a MinGW build of the server dll.
;
; The SDK's own dlls/hl.def cannot be used here: it ends with a
;
;     SECTIONS
;         .data READ WRITE
;
; clause that GNU ld's module-definition parser rejects outright.
;
; Only one export needs a definition file at all. Everything else the engine
; looks up by name -- GetEntityAPI, GetEntityAPI2, GetNewDLLFunctions and every
; entity classname registered by LINK_ENTITY_TO_CLASS -- is `cdecl` and carries
; `__declspec(dllexport)`, so MinGW exports it undecorated by itself.
;
; GiveFnptrsToDll is the exception. eiface.h makes it `__stdcall` on Windows and
; does not mark it exported, because MSVC took the export from the .def file.
; MinGW decorates a stdcall symbol as `name@bytes`, so the entry point would be
; exported as GiveFnptrsToDll@8 and the engine, which asks for
; "GiveFnptrsToDll", would find nothing and refuse to load the dll. The alias
; below exports the decorated symbol under the undecorated name.
LIBRARY hl
EXPORTS
	GiveFnptrsToDll = GiveFnptrsToDll@8 @1
